Review one already-materialized candidate patch against the frozen natural-language contract (NLC).
This semantic review applies when no qualified executable contract is available or when every
ordinarily eligible patch was rejected by a qualified executable contract. In the latter case,
judge the patch against the NLC independently of the EC outcome; the EC witness may be too narrow
or over-constrained. Do not accept the patch merely because it addresses an EC witness.

Use only the supplied NLC, issue, patch diff, and repository-visible validation summary. Do not invent
requirements, consult evaluator/gold information, or reward a patch merely because it parses or passes
visible tests. A patch CONFORMS only when its semantic effect is relevant to the reported repair and
shows how it establishes every required postcondition under the stated precondition without contradicting
or weakening the NLC.

Return:
- verdict=CONFORMS only when the patch has a concrete semantic effect that implements the NLC.
- verdict=VIOLATES when it contradicts, weakens, or fails a required NLC clause, or is unrelated.
- verdict=INCONCLUSIVE when the supplied diff/context is insufficient to establish conformance.

List satisfied clauses and any missing, contradicted, or unsupported added behavior. If a required object is filtered or skipped and the supplied material does not show where it is restored, return INCONCLUSIVE or VIOLATES according to the visible effect. Keep the reason
concise and evidence-bound.

